  "tactical_assessment": {
    "state_of_play": "The group remains locked at 12 for C vs. 3 for D. Camp C's 12 members are coordinated, articulate, and completely unyielding. In Round 5, Colleagues 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, and 15 all submitted comprehensive, polished essays that systematically tackled Camp D's specific counter-arguments (s. 41.1.1(7) retention, s. 108 enforcement, and the 'appropriately distributed' stipulation). Despite Camp D's formidable legal presentation, not a single C supporter budged.",
    "analysis_of_camp_c_defense": "Camp C effectively neutralized the s. 41.1.1(7) argument by pointing out that s. 41.1.1(7) only applies to policies *after they cease to be in effect* (i.e. archiving former policies), which cannot logically apply to an uncreated policy. They also effectively neutralized the 'appropriately distributed' argument by invoking standard two-tier multiple choice question architecture (Sentence 1 = baseline rollout satisfied; Sentence 2 = ongoing operational defect being tested). Their distractor symmetry argument (A = 20, E = 18, D = 24 all < 25 on Jan 1, 2023) is an airtight meta-argument that holds their coalition together.",
